<statement>
<p>
You are dealt one card from a standard deck of <m>\displaystyle{52}</m> playing cards. Find the probability of being dealt the following.</p>
<p>
(a)  A black card</p>
<p>
<fillin characters="20"/>   </p>
<p>
(b)  An odd diamond  (Note: We are only considering the number cards 2 through 10 as being odd; do NOT count the Ace.)</p>
<p>
<fillin characters="20"/>   </p>
<p>
(c)  The <m>\displaystyle{5}</m> of spades</p>
<p>
<fillin characters="20"/>   </p>
<p>
(d)  A red face card</p>
<p>
<fillin characters="20"/>   

</p>
</statement>
<answer>
<p><ul><li><m>\displaystyle\frac{{1}}{{2}}</m></li><li><m>\displaystyle\frac{{1}}{{13}}</m></li><li><m>\displaystyle\frac{{1}}{{52}}</m></li><li><m>\displaystyle\frac{{3}}{{26}}</m></li></ul></p>
</answer>

</myopenmath>